LICENSE	MPL-2.0
SPEC_WHAT_IT_IS	It is not a project in its own right: it is the template every new hyperpolymath\nrepository is created from. It ships CI/CD, machine-readable metadata\n(`.machine_readable/descriptiles/`), an AI gatekeeper deed\n(`rsr-template-repo_chora.deed`), a typed ABI/FFI seam (Idris2 over Zig), Guix and\nmise toolchains, and governance files, all passing the RSR validators before you\nadd a line of your own.
SPEC_USAGE	A person uses it to start a new repository:\n\n. On GitHub, *Use this template* (or clone it).\n. In the new checkout, run `just repo-init`. It asks for the project name, owner,\n  author and licence contact (listed in `.machine_readable/ai/PLACEHOLDERS.adoc`),\n  replaces every placeholder token, then validates the result. `just repo-init\n  julia-library` applies the one archetype overlay shipped in `archetypes/`.\n. Run `just validate` (structure + metadata) and `just doctor` (toolchain).\n\nAn AI running `repo-init` must pipe answers to stdin and must never set\n`RSR_NON_INTERACTIVE=1`: that stubs `read`, and the substitution loops then never end.
SPEC_PRIVACY	Nothing leaves the machine. `mise install` and `just setup` install tools per-user\nunder the mise data directory; `just repo-init` rewrites files only inside the\ncheckout. No remote repository is created and nothing is pushed until you do it.
SPEC_ARCHITECTURE	The template's own code is the ABI/FFI seam that every minted repo inherits:\n\n* `src/interface/Abi/` + `src/interface/abi.ipkg`: Idris2 types and layout proofs\n  (the ABI owns the contract).\n* `src/interface/ffi/`: the Zig implementation (`build.zig`, `src/main.zig`,\n  `test/integration_test.zig`), exporting C symbols named `<project>_*`.\n* `src/interface/generated/`: C headers generated from the ABI.\n\nEverything else is scaffolding: `.machine_readable/` (descriptiles, contractiles,\npolicies), `build/just/*.just` (the task phases the root `Justfile` imports), and\n`.github/workflows/` (the CI a minted repo starts with).
SPEC_DEV_COMMANDS	Template-specific commands:\n\n[source,bash]\n----\njust repo-init    # instantiate: fills every placeholder token, then validates\njust validate     # RSR shape + metadata + AI-install completeness\njust quality      # fmt-check, lint, test\njust test-all     # test, e2e, aspect, bench, readiness\njust repo-map     # regenerate docs/architecture/REPOSITORY-MAP.adoc (CI checks it)\n----\n\nThe golden path is `just test && just quality`. In the template itself `test` and\n`lint` fail on the placeholder tokens in `src/interface/ffi/src/main.zig`; that is\ndeliberate. Test a change to the FFI in a scratch copy after `repo-init`.
SPEC_LAYOUT	* Top level: `archetypes/ benches/ build/ ci/ docs/ examples/ features/ LICENSES/\n  scripts/ session/ src/ tests/ verification/ www/`. The root file list is fenced by\n  `.machine_readable/root-allow.txt`; a new root file needs a line there.\n* `build/just/`: provisioning (`provision.just`, `provision-lib.sh`), `repo-init.just`,\n  `validate.just`, and the other imported phases.\n* `build/guix.scm`, `build/manifest.scm`, `build/channels.scm`: the Guix route.\n* `tests/`: e2e, aspect, shape and workflow checks. `benches/`: benchmark harness.\n* `docs/`: SETUP, AI installation guide, onboarding warm-ups, architecture map.
SPEC_GOTCHAS	* `.machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile` must stay byte-identical to the root\n  `Justfile`; copy it after every edit.\n* Never put literal placeholder tokens in prose that `repo-init` will process: it\n  substitutes them. Write "placeholder token" instead.\n* `build/` is not an artefact directory here: `just clean` deliberately leaves it,\n  because `build/just/repo-init.just` lives there.\n* Descriptile and policy files are A2ML, which is retired: do not extend them or\n  build anything new on them.
